 ["All 1000-occurrence cases exceeded 120 seconds before completing warm-up; no large-case acceptance claim."
  "Retained scan prefix support/selection references grow quadratically: 5050 references for 100 scan occurrences. Numeric reductions are reused (99 invocations), but projection, comparison and provenance work remain expensive."
  "The 64-occurrence window retained 64 evidence payloads and 64 cache entries at N=100, but still had 100 premise states and 36 replay tombstones. Replay rejection metadata is intentionally not a fixed-size payload cache."
  "A window bounds occurrence identities, not the number of conflicting/alternative justifications for one identity; no adversarial byte bound is claimed."
  "Callables must be pure and closed over immutable bindings. Operator controls and lexical bindings are snapshotted at installation, not dynamically switched. Invocation templates retain the initial lexical network as setup state; fixtures install before publishing events."
  "Occurrence identities and semantic extents are stable in this experiment. Retiming an already discarded identity is outside the validated window contract."
  "Points and half-open constant intervals are supported. Only hold adds continuation. Continuous function segments and dynamic switching remain deferred."
